{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"scenario_analysis (by Lead Analyst):
{
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "case": "Bull",
   "probability": "20%",
   "driver": "A clean December 2026 response, 510(k) clearance in Q1 2027 and a CLIA waiver in 2028; the distributor converts its letter into the $2.4M opening order; hospital laboratories lift utilisation toward 4-8 panels a day.",
   "evidence": "41 paid sites with a 92% 90-day reorder rate; a five-analyte finger-stick cartridge no competitor offers; a pre-revenue point-of-care platform fetched a EUR 138M enterprise value in 2025 [S150, S204].",
   "outcome": "The FY2029 plan is met ($78.5M revenue, $9.0M profit) and a strategic sale at $450M-$550M in 2030-31 returns 2.4x-3.0x ($36M-$45M).",
   "implication": "Invest, but only with a sale-consent right, a cap on the Series A participation and a tranche tied to clearance."
  },
  {
   "case": "Base",
   "probability": "45%",
   "driver": "A second information request pushes clearance to H2 2027; launch is moderate-complexity and hospital-laboratory only; sites reach 120-180 by end-2028 and utilisation 2-3 panels a day.",
   "evidence": "66% of FY2025 510(k)s drew an information request, the average file needed 1.69 review cycles and total time averaged 141 days; no point-of-care troponin is CLIA-waived today [S266, S267, S17, S273].",
   "outcome": "Revenue of $25M-$35M by 2029 and a strategic sale at $180M-$300M in 2030-31 return 1.0x-1.55x ($15.0M-$23.3M).",
   "implication": "The return does not compensate the risk: wait for the clearance milestone or reprice the round."
  },
  {
   "case": "Bear",
   "probability": "35%",
   "driver": "The submission cannot be evidenced under the deck's identifier, a further FDA cycle follows, and a troponin CLIA waiver never arrives; cash ends in 2027-03 and the round prices down or the company sells assets.",
   "evidence": "K261734 is another company's cleared knee spacer [S193]; $6.9M of cash against $1.15M a month is 6.0 months to 2027-03-31; Cue Health filed Chapter 7 in 2024 after raising more than $480M [S150, S174].",
   "outcome": "An asset sale or recapitalisation at $30M-$80M pays Meridian $10.3M-$15.0M, 0.69x-1.0x.",
   "implication": "Pass at $140M pre-money: the 1x preference is the only protection and it still loses the time value of money."
  }
 ],
 "assumptions": [
  {
   "assumption": "Commercial utilisation reaches 8 panels a day per analyzer (16 a site) from 2028, against 1.02-1.37 observed across 55 evaluation analyzers.",
   "confidence": "low",
   "disproof": "The first cleared commercial cohort stays below 2 panels a day for two quarters.",
   "impact": "-60% to -85% of FY2029 revenue: 300 sites at observed utilisation produce $12.0M, not $78.5M.",
   "early_warning": "Cartridges per analyzer per month and reorder interval in the first 10 commercial sites."
  },
  {
   "assumption": "510(k) clearance arrives in Q1 2027 and a CLIA waiver is granted by 2028.",
   "confidence": "low",
   "disproof": "The FDA acknowledgment letter shows a different submission number, or a second information request arrives in Q1 2027.",
   "impact": "A 12-month slip adds $16.5M to the FY2027 loss and forces a bridge or down round; equity value roughly halves.",
   "early_warning": "Completeness of the December 2026 response; FDA database status under the correct number."
  },
  {
   "assumption": "$140M pre-money and a 1x participating Series A with no disclosed cap.",
   "confidence": "high",
   "disproof": "The charter shows a participation cap or a non-participating Series A.",
   "impact": "At $100M pre-money the same $15M buys 11.5% and the 3x threshold falls from $546M to $426M; a cap releases about $25M to other holders at a $170M exit.",
   "early_warning": "Series A agreements and the restated charter in the data room."
  },
  {
   "assumption": "Unit cost falls from $16.20 to $7.50 at 2M cartridges a year (126 times 2026 volume).",
   "confidence": "low",
   "disproof": "Supplier quotes or the bill of materials show a reagent and antibody floor above $9, or scrap above 3%.",
   "impact": "At a $10 unit cost FY2029 gross profit falls by $6.3M, from $55.7M to $49.4M.",
   "early_warning": "Quotes for antibodies and reagents; pilot-line yield and scrap rates."
  },
  {
   "assumption": "FY2026E of $5.9M includes a $2.4M stocking order that ships only after clearance, so underlying FY2026 is $3.5M.",
   "confidence": "high",
   "disproof": "A firm purchase order with delivery before 2026-12-31.",
   "impact": "-41% of FY2026 revenue; 2027 growth is partly a shipment rather than demand, and 5.8 months of channel inventory against a nine-month shelf life carries return and expiry risk.",
   "early_warning": "Purchase order and shipment terms; distributor inventory levels."
  }
 ],
 "consensus": {
  "consensus": "The company and its insiders price the round as if clearance, the waiver and the 300-site ramp were de-risked: Q1 2027 clearance, 300 sites by end-2027, 8 panels a day, $78.5M of FY2029 revenue and a $400M-plus exit. The $140M pre-money and the 12.2% step-up over the 2022 Series A encode that view, and the deck's opening page asks diligence tools to accept it without verification.",
  "our_view": "No edge on the price. The probability-weighted value is $115M-$132M, 22%-32% below the $170M post-money, and the new money returns 1.0x across most plausible exits. The thesis differs on utilisation (1.02-1.37 panels a day observed against 8 modelled) and on the regulatory record (the deck's 510(k) number belongs to another company's device).",
  "evidence": "Observed utilisation across 55 analyzers, the CMS rates for the five codes ($71.32 full panel against $12.47 for troponin alone), the FDA record for K261734, and the waterfall showing 1.0x from $36.3M to $196.7M [S150, S177, S193, S8, S213, S214].",
  "proof_event": "The FDA acknowledgment letter for the actual submission number and information request, followed by the first cleared commercial cohort's cartridges per analyzer per month."
 },
 "one_question": {
  "question": "What submission number does FDA's acknowledgment letter show, and what did the 2026-08-21 information request ask for?",
  "why": "The deck's identifier is another company's cleared knee spacer, so the Q1 2027 clearance, the $2.4M order, the 2027 launch and the valuation all rest on a filing no public record supports. If the submission is real and the request is narrow, the base case holds at a lower price; if it is not, the bear case is the case."
 },
 "modules": {
  "analogs": "Cue Health (cautionary): raised more than $480M and listed on Nasdaq, then filed Chapter 7 on 2024-05-28 — capital and a consumer brand did not substitute for reimbursement and regulatory durability. LumiraDx (cautionary): entered pre-pack administration on 2023-12-29 and its point-of-care technology sold to Roche for $295M plus up to $55M — the technology kept option value while the equity did not. QuidelOrtho/LEX Diagnostics (best): $100M cash in 2026 for a cleared, CLIA-waived point-of-care asset — the price anchor for what Vantelle is trying to become. bioMerieux/SpinChip (best): EUR 138M enterprise value in 2025 for a pre-revenue point-of-care platform — proof that strategics pay before revenue, but at a platform price, not a franchise price.",
  "capital_efficiency": "$51.5M raised ($46.5M equity and $5.0M debt) has produced $2.6M of FY2025 revenue, $0.05 per dollar raised, and $58.7M of cumulative losses over FY2024-FY2028E. The burn multiple is 8.3x in FY2025 and 15.6x in FY2026 excluding the stocking order, revenue per employee is $40,625 on 64 staff, and the plan consumes the $30M before its first profit year. The category base rate is unforgiving: Cue Health raised more than $480M before Chapter 7, Truvian has raised $225.3M while still funding clearance, and LumiraDx sold its technology only after a revenue collapse [S150, S174, S175].",
  "position_sizing": "Private, so there is no Kelly fraction. Do not lead at $140M pre-money. At $95M-$110M pre-money, a $10M-$12M check with $10M reserved for a clearance tranche and $20M-plus held for a Series C keeps the entry inside the precedent band; conditions are the FDA acknowledgment letter, a cap on the Series A participation, a sale-consent right for the new lead and a full-time CFO before close. At $140M the recommendation is to pass or wait for the 510(k) decision, then reprice."
 },
 "author": "Lead Analyst",
 "saved_at": "2026-10-30T05:02:21+00:00"
}"}],"isError":false}

